aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg>Compare</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/glossary\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-book-open h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 7v14\"></path><path d=\"M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z\"></path></svg>Glossary</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/blog\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-book-open h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 7v14\"></path><path d=\"M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z\"></path></svg>Blog</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/salary\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-trending-up h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 7h6v6\"></path><path d=\"m22 7-8.5 8.5-5-5L2 17\"></path></svg>Salary</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/tax-data\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Data</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/widgets\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg>Widgets</a></nav><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><a class=\"hidden sm:flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Calculate Now</a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:bg-accent dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 rounded-md gap-1.5 px-3 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 lg:hidden text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground\" aria-label=\"Toggle mobile menu\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 18h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 6h16\"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id=\"main-content\" class=\"flex-1\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/louisiana-tax-calculator#webpage\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/louisiana-tax-calculator\",\"name\":\"Louisiana Tax Calculator 2026\",\"description\":\"Free Louisiana tax calculator 2026. Take-home pay after 1.85%–4.25% state income tax. Progressive income tax. Top rate 4.25% above $50,000.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-06-25\",\"author\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com#author\"},\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#organization\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/louisiana-tax-calculator#breadcrumb\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Louisiana Tax Calculator\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/louisiana-tax-calculator\"}]},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/louisiana-tax-calculator#webapp\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"Louisiana Tax Calculator\",\"applicationCategory\":\"FinanceApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Web\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":0,\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"availability\":\"https://schema.org/InStock\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/louisiana-tax-calculator\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/louisiana-tax-calculator#faq\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How is my take-home pay calculated?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Your take-home pay is what's left after three main deductions come out of your gross salary. First, federal income tax applies using progressive brackets (10%–37%) after subtracting the standard deduction and any pre-tax contributions. Second, FICA takes 7.65% for Social Security (6.2%, capped at $184,500 in 2026) and Medicare (1.45%, no cap). Third, your state income tax is calculated based on your state's own brackets and deductions — which vary widely, from 0% in states like Texas and Florida to over 13% in California. Subtract all three, and what's left is your take-home pay.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is FICA and why is it deducted from my paycheck?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"FICA stands for Federal Insurance Contributions Act, and it funds two major programs: Social Security and Medicare. You pay 6.2% of your wages for Social Security (capped at $184,500 in earnings for 2026) and 1.45% for Medicare with no income cap. That's 7.65% total coming out of every paycheck. Your employer matches that amount on their end, but you only see your 7.65% on your pay stub. If you earn over $200,000, there's an additional 0.9% Medicare surcharge on everything above that threshold. Unlike federal and state income taxes, FICA is not reduced by pre-tax contributions like 401(k) — only HSA and some other specific deductions can lower it.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does this calculator account for 401(k) and HSA contributions?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Traditional 401(k) contributions reduce your taxable income for both federal and state income tax purposes, which lowers the income tax withheld from each paycheck. For 2026, you can contribute up to $24,500 to a 401(k) ($32,500 if you're 50+, and even more with the 60–63 catch-up). HSA contributions also reduce your taxable income — the 2026 limit is $4,300 for individual coverage or $8,550 for family. Note that neither 401(k) nor HSA contributions reduce FICA taxes, only income taxes. Roth 401(k) contributions are made after-tax, so they don't reduce your current taxable income but grow tax-free.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How does filing status affect my paycheck?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Your filing status determines your standard deduction and tax brackets, which directly impacts how much federal tax is withheld from each paycheck. For 2026, the standard deduction is $16,100 for single filers, $32,200 for married filing jointly, and $24,150 for head of household. A higher standard deduction means less taxable income and less tax withheld. Married filing jointly generally results in the lowest tax burden because the brackets are exactly double the single brackets, and the standard deduction is twice as large. Head of household falls in between. Your filing status also affects state taxes in most states that have an income tax.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is this calculator accurate for 2026?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. This calculator uses the official 2026 federal tax brackets, standard deductions, and FICA rates published by the IRS, along with the most current state income tax brackets, deductions, and exemptions for each state. The federal brackets are adjusted annually for inflation, and the 2026 standard deduction is $16,100 for single filers, $32,200 for married filing jointly, and $24,150 for head of household. While the calculator provides accurate estimates based on these rates, it may not account for every possible deduction, credit, or special situation — for a complete tax picture, consult a tax professional.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the difference between effective and marginal tax rate?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Your marginal tax rate is the rate applied to your last dollar of income — essentially the highest bracket you fall into. Your effective tax rate is your total tax divided by your total income, which gives you an overall average. For example, a single filer making $75,000 has a marginal rate of 22%, but because the first $11,600 is taxed at 10%, the next chunk at 12%, and only the amount above $47,150 at 22%, their effective federal rate is closer to 11–12%. The effective rate is what actually matters for understanding your overall tax burden, while the marginal rate tells you how much tax you'd save with each dollar of deduction.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do state taxes affect my take-home pay?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"State income taxes can make a significant difference in your take-home pay, and the gap between states is massive. Nine states (Alaska, Florida, Nevada, New Hampshire, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Washington, and Wyoming) charge no state income tax on wages. On the other end, California's top rate hits 13.3%. For a $100,000 salary, living in a no-tax state versus California could mean a difference of over $6,000 per year in take-home pay. Most states fall somewhere in between, with effective rates ranging from 2% to 7% for middle-income earners. Some states use flat rates (like Illinois at 4.95%) while most use progressive brackets similar to the federal system.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are there additional local taxes not shown here?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, some cities and counties levy additional income taxes that this calculator may not include. The most notable example is New York City, which charges its own income tax of roughly 3.1%–3.9% on top of New York State's tax. Other cities with local income taxes include Philadelphia (about 3.75%), Detroit, and various municipalities in Ohio, Pennsylvania, Indiana, and Kentucky. Additionally, some states allow local school district taxes or occupational license fees. If you live in one of these areas, your actual take-home pay may be lower than what this calculator shows. Check your local government's website for any additional withholding requirements.\"}}]},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Rachel Mitchell\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"jobTitle\":\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director, CPA\",\"description\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\",\"knowsAbout\":[\"Federal Income Tax\",\"State Income Tax\",\"FICA Tax\",\"Payroll Tax\",\"IRS Compliance\",\"Tax Planning\",\"Multi-State Taxation\",\"Tax-Advantaged Accounts\"],\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachelmitchellcpa/\",\"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/\"],\"worksFor\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"image\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\"}]}</script><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><a class=\"hover:text-foreground transition-colors\" href=\"/\">Home</a><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\" aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span class=\"text-foreground font-medium\">Louisiana</span></nav><div class=\"mb-4 flex justify-center\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-muted-foreground\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2 h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"5\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"19\" r=\"3\"></circle><line x1=\"8.59\" x2=\"15.42\" y1=\"13.51\" y2=\"17.49\"></line><line x1=\"15.41\" x2=\"8.59\" y1=\"6.51\" y2=\"10.49\"></line></svg>Share:</span><a href=\"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=Louisiana%20Tax%20Calculator%202026%20%7C%201.85-4.75%25%20Progressive&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fthetaxcalc.com%2Flouisiana-tax-calculator&amp;via=TheTaxCalc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/30 p-2 transition-all hover:bg-sky-500/10 hover:text-sky-400 hover:border-sky-500/30\" aria-label=\"Share on Twitter / X\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-twitter h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M22 4s-.7 2.1-2 3.4c1.6 10-9.4 17.3-18 11.6 2.2.1 4.4-.6 6-2C3 15.5.5 9.6 3 5c2.2 2.6 5.6 4.1 9 4-.9-4.2 4-6.6 7-3.8 1.1 0 3-1.2 3-1.2z\"></path></svg></a><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthetaxcalc.com%2Flouisiana-tax-calculator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/30 p-2 transition-all hover:bg-blue-500/10 hover:text-blue-400 hover:border-blue-500/30\" aria-label=\"Share on LinkedIn\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-linkedin h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 8a6 6 0 0 1 6 6v7h-4v-7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7h-4v-7a6 6 0 0 1 6-6z\"></path><rect width=\"4\" height=\"12\" x=\"2\" y=\"9\"></rect><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2\"></circle></svg></a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"justify-center whitespace-nowrap font-medium disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:text-accent-foreground dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/30 px-3 py-2 text-xs transition-all hover:bg-muted/50\" aria-label=\"Copy link\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link2 lucide-link-2 h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M9 17H7A5 5 0 0 1 7 7h2\"></path><path d=\"M15 7h2a5 5 0 1 1 0 10h-2\"></path><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"16\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"12\"></line></svg>Copy Link</button></div></div><div class=\"mb-8 text-center\"><h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl\">Free Louisiana Tax Calculator</h1><p class=\"mt-2 text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto\">Calculate your 2026 Louisiana take-home pay after progressive state tax (1.85%–4.75%), federal tax &amp; FICA. No sign-up.</p><p class=\"mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Last reviewed: January 2026 · Tax data verified against IRS Publication 15-T &amp; state revenue departments</p></div><!--$!--><template data-dgst=\"BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING\"></template><div class=\"space-y-6\"><div class=\"grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-5\"><div class=\"space-y-4 lg:col-span-3\"><div class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-6 w-40 mb-4\"></div><div class=\"space-y-4\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-2/3\"></div></div></div></div><div class=\"lg:col-span-2\"><div class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-6 w-32 mb-4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-20 w-full mb-4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-3/4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-1/2\"></div></div></div></div></div><!--/$--><div id=\"scenario-comparison\" class=\"mt-8\"><div id=\"scenario-comparison\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><div data-state=\"closed\" data-slot=\"collapsible\"><div data-slot=\"card\" class=\"text-card-foreground flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-xl border py-6 shadow-sm border-blue-500/20 bg-card/80 backdrop-blur-sm\"><div data-slot=\"collapsible-trigger\" class=\"@container/card-header grid auto-rows-min grid-rows-[auto_auto] items-start gap-1.5 px-6 has-data-[slot=card-action]:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] [.border-b]:pb-6 cursor-pointer pb-4 transition-colors hover:bg-muted/30\" type=\"button\" aria-controls=\"radix-_R_6av5uhtb_\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-state=\"closed\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-5 w-5 text-blue-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg><div data-slot=\"card-title\" class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">Compare Tax Scenarios</div><span data-slot=\"badge\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border px-2 py-0.5 font-medium w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden [a&amp;]:hover:bg-accent [a&amp;]:hover:text-accent-foreground text-xs border-blue-500/30 text-blue-400\">New</span></div><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground transition-transform\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></div><div data-slot=\"card-description\" class=\"text-muted-foreground text-sm\">Compare up to 4 scenarios side by side — different states, 401(k) contributions, or filing statuses</div></div><div data-state=\"closed\" id=\"radix-_R_6av5uhtb_\" hidden=\"\" data-slot=\"collapsible-content\"></div></div></div></div></div><section class=\"mt-8 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3\">Related Tools &amp; Resources</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2\"><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/compare\"><span>📊</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Compare States</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Side-by-side tax comparison</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/salary\"><span>💰</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Salary After Tax</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Take-home pay by salary level</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/glossary\"><span>📖</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Tax Glossary</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Key tax terms explained</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/blog\"><span>📝</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Tax Guides</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Expert tips and guides</p></div></a></div></section><div class=\"mt-12 space-y-10\"><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">How This Calculator Works</h2><div class=\"space-y-4\"><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Louisiana income tax rate: 1.85%–4.25%. Progressive income tax. Top rate 4.25% above $50,000. This means your paycheck in Louisiana is only reduced by federal income tax and FICA — plus state tax at 4.25% top rate.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The 2026 federal tax brackets apply the same way in Louisiana as everywhere else: 10%–37% progressive rates after the $16,100 standard deduction (single) or $32,200 (married). FICA adds 6.2% Social Security (up to $184,500) + 1.45% Medicare.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Louisiana has a progressive income tax ranging from 1.85%–4.25%. Louisiana has one of the highest combined sales tax rates (9.55%) but very low property taxes (0.55%). On a $75,000 salary (single filer), your take-home pay is approximately $59,950 per year after federal tax, FICA, and state income tax.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Louisiana also has a 4.45% state (9.55% avg combined) sales tax and 0.55% average effective property tax rate. Louisiana has one of the highest combined sales tax rates (9.55%) but very low property taxes (0.55%).</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Use the calculator above to see your exact take-home pay in Louisiana. Enter your salary, filing status, and any pre-tax deductions to get an instant, accurate result — no sign-up required.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">How It&#x27;s Calculated</h2><div class=\"space-y-5\"><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Formula</h3><div class=\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\">Net Pay = Gross Income − (Federal Tax + State Tax + FICA)</div></div><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Step-by-Step</h3><ol class=\"space-y-2\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">1</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Apply Louisiana progressive income tax (1.85%–4.25%)</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">2</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Subtract pre-tax deductions (401(k), HSA) from gross pay</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">3</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Apply federal standard deduction ($16,100 single / $32,200 married)</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">4</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Calculate federal tax using progressive brackets (10%–37%)</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">5</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Calculate FICA: 6.2% Social Security (up to $184,500) + 1.45% Medicare</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">6</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Subtract all taxes from gross pay to get net take-home pay</span></li></ol></div><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Example</h3><div class=\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">$75000 salary, single in Louisiana: Federal tax ≈ $7,670. FICA = $5,738. State tax varies. Net ≈ $59,950/year.</div></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">For detailed data sources and full methodology, see our <a class=\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\" href=\"/methodology\">Methodology &amp; Data Sources</a> page.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Key Rates &amp; Data for 2026</h2><div class=\"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\"><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">Louisiana Income Tax</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">1.85%–4.25%</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">Louisiana Sales Tax</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">4.45% state (9.55% avg combined)</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">Louisiana Property Tax</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">0.55%</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">Federal Standard Deduction</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">$16,100 (single)</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">FICA Social Security</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">6.2% (up to $184,500)</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class=\"space-y-3\"><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Does Louisiana have a state income tax?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Yes. Louisiana has a progressive income tax ranging from 1.85%–4.25%. Progressive income tax. Top rate 4.25% above $50,000.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">What is the tax rate in Louisiana?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Louisiana has a 1.85%–4.25% income tax rate, 4.45% state (9.55% avg combined) sales tax, and 0.55% average property tax rate. Louisiana has one of the highest combined sales tax rates (9.55%) but very low property taxes (0.55%).</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">How much is $75,000 after taxes in Louisiana?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">On a $75,000 salary in Louisiana (single filer), your take-home pay is approximately $59,950 per year. This includes federal tax (~$7,670), FICA (~$5,738), and state income tax. Your monthly take-home would be about $4,996.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Is Louisiana a tax-friendly state?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Louisiana has a 4.25% top income tax rate, which is among the lowest in the nation. Combined with 4.45% state (9.55% avg combined) sales tax and 0.55% property tax, the overall tax burden is relatively low compared to other states.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Does Louisiana tax retirement income?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Louisiana taxes retirement income as part of your regular income at the 1.85%–4.25% rate. Some states exempt Social Security or pension income — check with a tax professional for your specific situation.</div></details></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\"><p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-4\">Related Calculators</p><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Paycheck Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/texas-tax-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Texas Calculator (0% tax)</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/florida-tax-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Florida Calculator (0% tax)</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" 