0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Louisiana income tax rate: 1.85%–4.25%. Progressive income tax. Top rate 4.25% above $50,000. This means your paycheck in Louisiana is only reduced by federal income tax and FICA — plus state tax at 4.25% top rate.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"The 2026 federal tax brackets apply the same way in Louisiana as everywhere else: 10%–37% progressive rates after the $16,100 standard deduction (single) or $32,200 (married). FICA adds 6.2% Social Security (up to $184,500) + 1.45% Medicare.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Louisiana has a progressive income tax ranging from 1.85%–4.25%. Louisiana has one of the highest combined sales tax rates (9.55%) but very low property taxes (0.55%). On a $75,000 salary (single filer), your take-home pay is approximately $59,950 per year after federal tax, FICA, and state income tax.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Louisiana also has a 4.45% state (9.55% avg combined) sales tax and 0.55% average effective property tax rate. Louisiana has one of the highest combined sales tax rates (9.55%) but very low property taxes (0.55%).\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Use the calculator above to see your exact take-home pay in Louisiana. Enter your salary, filing status, and any pre-tax deductions to get an instant, accurate result — no sign-up required.\\\"}}]]}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How It's Calculated\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Formula\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Net Pay = Gross Income − (Federal Tax + State Tax + FICA)\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Step-by-Step\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"ol\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\\\",\\\"children\\\":1}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Apply Louisiana progressive income tax (1.85%–4.25%)\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\\\",\\\"children\\\":2}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Subtract pre-tax deductions (401(k), HSA) from gross pay\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"classNa