ogressive rates after the $16,100 standard deduction (single) or $32,200 (married). FICA adds 6.2% Social Security (up to $184,500) + 1.45% Medicare.\"}}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Louisiana has a progressive income tax ranging from 1.85%–4.25%. Louisiana has one of the highest combined sales tax rates (9.55%) but very low property taxes (0.55%). On a $75,000 salary (single filer), your take-home pay is approximately $59,950 per year after federal tax, FICA, and state income tax.\"}}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Louisiana also has a 4.45% state (9.55% avg combined) sales tax and 0.55% average effective property tax rate. Louisiana has one of the highest combined sales tax rates (9.55%) but very low property taxes (0.55%).\"}}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Use the calculator above to see your exact take-home pay in Louisiana. Enter your salary, filing status, and any pre-tax deductions to get an instant, accurate result — no sign-up required.\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"How It's Calculated\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"Formula\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Net Pay = Gross Income − (Federal Tax + State Tax + FICA)\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm 